WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.963 --> 00:00:04.213
(dramatic piano music)

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:08.670
- [Jana] Women on
television and local news,

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.960
they have really cool, like,
Rent the Runway dresses.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:12.860
They're beautiful.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:15.230
They know how to do their makeup,

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:17.410
like they were born to know.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:21.173
They have lots of earrings and tall shoes.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.049
I wanted to be them my whole life,

00:00:24.049 --> 00:00:27.817
'cause if I got to be
them, or look like them,

00:00:27.817 --> 00:00:30.710
that was the ultimate hall pass.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.620
I could just tell stories.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.970
And I maxed out a lot of credit cards

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.330
trying to look like that.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.400
But this is the one we've
all been waiting for.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.610
It just didn't work.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:41.960
Good evening, I'm Jana Shortal.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.160
Thank you for joining us.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:44.830
You can't have an authentic voice

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.823
if you feel like you're in a costume.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:51.300
It took a long time, but I did find a way

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.565
to unapologetically be myself.

00:00:53.565 --> 00:00:56.565
(piano music slows)

00:01:04.486 --> 00:01:07.903
(string plucking music)

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:10.310
My name is Jana Shortal.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.040
I'm a journalist, and I host a show here

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:13.990
at KARE 11 in Minneapolis, Minnesota.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.760
Are you guys excited?

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:16.900
When I first moved to Minneapolis

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.150
15 years ago, I was not out.

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:20.895
I didn't see anyone succeeding

00:01:20.895 --> 00:01:24.120
in front of a camera as a gay woman.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.720
You know, I remember being a little kid

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:29.200
when Ellen came out,
and it didn't go well.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:33.645
Rachel Maddow wasn't on TV
back then, so I swallowed it.

00:01:33.645 --> 00:01:35.723
The first thing I did
when I moved here was

00:01:35.723 --> 00:01:39.260
get boyfriend, and he's great.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:40.850
I haven't really seen him in 15 years,

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.145
so I still like you, Craig.

00:01:43.145 --> 00:01:43.978
(laughs)

00:01:43.978 --> 00:01:48.760
I was actively internally
fighting the fact that I was gay.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:51.338
It was like being two
being two people at once,

00:01:51.338 --> 00:01:53.373
but you can only do that for so long.

00:01:56.565 --> 00:01:59.260
(dramatic piano music)

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:03.376
As a girl growing up in the
world, there was a code.

00:02:03.376 --> 00:02:07.080
And in this industry, at least the code

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:10.070
was very easy to see and follow.

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.760
Pretty hair, perfect
makeup, and their outfits

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.540
look like they do in the magazines.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:15.520
Look at my face.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:16.353
Look at my face.

00:02:16.353 --> 00:02:18.193
Look how there's no lesbian smirk yet.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:25.583
That was internally difficult,
but I knew how to do it.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:30.860
So in my late 20s, I started coming

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:33.360
out a little bit at a time.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.820
I'm not out on air, and when I would have

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.760
to be on this side of the
camera, I got so scared.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.830
It was where I was least confident

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.305
'cause I would have to do stuff

00:02:42.305 --> 00:02:44.050
to look like somebody I wasn't,

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:47.010
and how can you authentically
present the news

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:49.163
or someone's story when you're terrified?

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.657
Someone said, "Cut you hair.

00:02:52.657 --> 00:02:54.007
"This isn't working."

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:58.840
It went from bob to short by Kimberly.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:02.923
Kimberly, Kim, helped
me to become who I am.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.490
- I've been doing Jana's
hair for about 15 years.

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:13.580
When I first met her, she
needed a beautifully executed,

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:16.750
masterful bob, but I would style her hair

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.681
differently in order
to go out with friends

00:03:19.681 --> 00:03:22.330
than we would if she
was going back to work,

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:23.950
and the two became very separate.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:25.930
It was two Janas, and for
me, it was overwhelming

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:27.810
because it was two clients.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.212
We worked together to help her evolve

00:03:30.212 --> 00:03:35.212
into what is now her most
comfortable personal style.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.703
As she was assigned this new
project and this new show,

00:03:37.703 --> 00:03:40.240
it became more evident to me that

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.760
that was what they were wanting to see.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.010
They were wanting to see more of her,

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:46.738
and so I absolutely was
banging a tambourine

00:03:46.738 --> 00:03:50.003
trying to cheer her on and
trying to move it right along.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.740
I love her coming out story.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:54.253
I think it's beautiful.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:59.780
- When we debuted this show
on January 11th of 2016,

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:03.500
I felt confident enough to wear this hair

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:07.220
and a David Bowie t-shirt,
and I was so scared

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:09.090
that the minute I got
off there would be, like,

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.660
this group of people that
were gonna beat me up,

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.571
or, like, send me mail to
say, "Take her off the air."

00:04:13.571 --> 00:04:15.550
None of that happened.

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:17.360
The applause were there.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:20.426
I wasn't saying, "I'm going to
be this, like, trailblazer."

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.720
I'm just me.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.735
I mean, this is always who I've been.

00:04:23.735 --> 00:04:26.234
I'm sad that I'm some sort of anomaly.

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:28.300
It seems goofy because
I know a lot of people

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.670
that look like me, but
I'm sure you could call

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:31.850
news directors all over the country

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:33.600
that would say my hair's a problem.

00:04:35.612 --> 00:04:38.490
(uplifting electric guitar music)

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.726
We all know the heartbreaking stories

00:04:40.726 --> 00:04:44.460
about what happens in the LGBTQ community

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:47.363
to kids figuring out where you belong.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.276
And I will be damned
if I am not the person

00:04:51.276 --> 00:04:54.083
that they need me to be to get them

00:04:54.083 --> 00:04:56.530
(yelling)
to that point where they see

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:58.633
themselves and say, "Hell yeah."

